## SUCCESS CRITERIA

The Shock Calibration POC must support:

1. Controlled historical Olympus data downloads.
2. Correct market-factor identification and mapping.
3. Financially appropriate data-quality validation.
4. Local historical storage using Parquet and DuckDB.
5. Reusable deterministic quantitative calculations.
6. A genuinely conversational LLM interface.
7. Open-ended questions across locally available market factors.
8. Configurable historical periods and rolling windows.
9. Source-grounded numerical results and clear limitations.
10. Extension to additional asset classes without architectural redesign.

**The central principle: Olympus supplies historical data; the local analytical platform performs the calculations; the LLM makes the platform conversational.**

Begin by consolidating the existing project and validating the historical data foundation. Then continue implementation without restarting previous work.
